-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Workgroup Solutions, Inc. has announced a beta program for a full featured
Linux-ELF business accounting package.  AcctOnIt is a port of a popular
DOS/Clipper-based accounting package ported to Linux with Flagship,
Workgroup Solutions' Linux-native dBase/Clipper compatible development
environment.

The AcctOnIt beta modules can be downloaded at:

ftp://www.wgs.com/pub/wgs/acctonit

The beta will run until bug reports stop.  For those interested in
participating, bugs should be reported to fstech@wgs.com.  Persons who
participate actively in the beta will be allowed to keep their most recent
download free of charge after the beta is terminated.  Thereafter, the
GL/Sysadmin modules will be available for download, and the remaining
modules can be purchased for $199/module.

WGS is in the process of making a mailing list available for AcctOnIt beta
testers.  Subscription information will be posted here when the list is
ready.

I do not work for WGS.  I'm a beta tester of AcctOnIt, and I like it.  I
want to see it succeed.

 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[ Moderator's note: The following arrived later. I include it
  here instead of posting it as a separate message for reasons of 
  brevity. --liw ]

Be advised that as of 1/23/97, the Accounts Receivable module is missing
from the WGS download site.  I have emailed WGS regarding the issue.  The
filename is acctar.lzh.  If you have downloaded the beta modules and that
file is missing, please check the site again.

Also be advised that the beta install routine is a little quirky.  It will
delete the distribution files from the install directory upon successful
completion *or abort*.  Be sure to keep a copy of the distribution files in
a safe place in case you have to reinstall.

Mike

