BALUG (The Bay Area Linux Users Group) announces a new MAILING LIST for
San Francisco Bay area Linux users.

The list is meant for discussions regarding BALUG, and also to provide
interchange and problem-solving expertise between linux enthusiasts,
inside and outside of the bay area.

To subscribe, send a message to balug-request@sifry.com with the word
"subscribe" (minus the quotes) in the body of the message.

A digest version of the list is also available.

To subscribe to the digest, send a message to
balug-digest-request@sifry.com with the word "subscribe" (minus the
quotes) in the body of the message.

Join in and help shape the future of BALUG, make some new friends, and
get some top-notch linux advice and help.

The February meeting of BALUG is on Tuesday, February 4th, 1997 in the
upper banquet room of the Four Seas Restaurant, on 731 Grant Avenue in
San Francisco.

Easy parking is available at a city garage located at the corner of 
Kearny and Commercial. (across from the Chinatown Holiday Inn on
Kearny)  
Parking in the area varies- street parking IS available in the area.  
Arrive early!  Doors open at 6:30!

We have an excellent evening planned for you and are very proud to 
present our speaker, Dr. Neil J. Gunther, an internationally recognized 
expert in performance management and capacity planning.  We are honored 
to have him as our first guest speaker for 1997.  Casual and
professional users alike will not want to miss this presentation!  We
can assure youll have a great time, well worth the trip into the city. 
In addition, youll have the opportunity to ask Dr. Gunther questions,
network for jobs or information, and enjoy a fantastic repast.

RSVP!  If you have not come to one of our meetings- you're really
missing out.  Send reservations to aftyde@aol.com.   Please let us know
in advance if you require a special menu.  

RSVP for DINNER, MEETING or BOTH to Art Tyde at aftyde@aol.com

- -- 
