4th International Linux Congress: Announcement and  Call For Papers

The 4th International Linux Kongress 1997 will be held from May 21. to May
23. at the Hofstuben Tagungszentrum, Festung Marienberg in W=FCrzburg. It
follows the tradition of the Linux conference series (Heidelberg 94 and
Berlin 95/96) which has evolved into the most important meeting for Linux
experts, developers and users.

The conference will offer up to 30 talks on two days in two parallel
tracks. The first track is dedicated to Linux development, the second
track is intended to accomodate talks about Linux applications and usage.
Each talk will be 40 minutes (possibly including discussion). The language
of the talks will be English or German.

In addition, there will be two workshops on kernel development and XFree86
server development on May 21 in the afternoon.

For participants, interested in a particular topic, we offer additional
informal gatherings (Birds-of-a-Feather sessions). BoFs may be scheduled
at the conference or in advance by mailing the program chair.

In order to provide the best possible talk offerings, we solicit proposals
for new talks. Questions regarding a topic's relevance to the conference
may be addressed to the program chair via email to
chair@linux-kongress.de. An abstract (1 page) is required for the
selection process. The preferred form of submission is via electronic mail
to the program chair.

Submissions must be recieved by January 31st 1997 latest.=20

For distribution to the participants, an extended abstract or a full paper
must be provided by February 28, 1997. It is required that papers will not
have been previously published elsewhere.=20

The conference will be organized by GUUG (Association of German Unix
Users), LunetIX and Thinking Objects and supported by several companies
(Fachbuchhandlung Lehmanns, Addison-Wesley, O'Reilly, dpunkt Verlag).  Any
profits from this event will be used to support Free-Software-Projects.

The complete program and registration information will be available in
March 1997. If you would like to receive
registration materials, please contact the GUUG office:=20

