Jcd: Java CD Audio Player 1.0
Caching Client for Xmcd cddb servers
- ------------------------------------
Java Application for Linux - requires JDK - doesn't work with Netscape.

Jcd is currently at
  ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/jcd-1.0.tar.gz
  ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/jcd-1.0.lsm
  (final location should be ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/apps/sound/cds)

Screen shot online at http://www.actrix.gen.nz/users/michael/

Jcd uses the Xmcd cddb database format and protocols courtesy of Ti Kan
and Steve Scherf (http://sunsite.unc.edu/~cddb/xmcd).

I CAN'T PROMISE TO SUPPORT OR ENHANCE JCD, BUT FEEDBACK IS WELCOME.

I'm quite happy for others to take jcd and carry it in new directions.
For example, the Xmcd cddb client object could be extracted and put to
other uses.  The low and intermediate level CD drive interfaces could
also be easily reused.  At a lower level the FancyButton object might
be useful.

I developed Jcd using JDK 1.0.2, Linux 2.0.20, Caldera 1.0, Redhat
3.0.3, Xemacs 19.14.  It will probably port easily to any platform
that supports Sun's CDROM IOCTL calls, for other platforms you would
need to rewrite one low level module in either Java or C.

Here is the Linux LSM entry:

