Academic Pricing for NExS Personal Edition Introduced
- -----------------------------------------------------
X Engineering Software Systems (XESS Corp.) announces the immediate
availability of academic pricing for the Personal Edition of its NExS
spreadsheet for UNIX and Linux workstations.

XESS Corp. President Tom Miller stated:

     We originally instituted academic pricing only for our NExS
     Professional Edition with floating license management. This forced
     our academic customers to install the FLEX license manager
     software just to take advantage of our lower academic prices, even
     if they were buying only a single copy of NExS. Now by extending
     academic pricing to our Personal Edition of NExS, academic
     customers can buy a small number of licenses at lower costs and
     have a much simpler installation process.

A Demo Edition of the NExS spreadsheet can be downloaded from www.xess.com
along with a free 30-day trial license that's valid on HP/UX, AIX, Digital
UNIX, SunOS, Solaris and Linux platforms.



Free 30-Day Trial Licenses for NExS
- -----------------------------------
X Engineering Software Systems (XESS Corp.) announces the immediate
availability of free 30-day trial licenses for its NExS spreadsheet for UNIX
and Linux workstations.

XESS Corp. President Tom Miller stated:

     Our original NExS Demo Edition had no time limit on its use, but
     it did limit people to using just twenty-five active spreadsheet
     cells. Now they can get a free license that unlocks the full
     capabilities of NExS for thirty days. This will help those who
     were previously trying to ``stress test'' NExS but were unable to
     process large sheets because of the cell limit. Now they can
     evaluate NExS in its true form.

The 30-day trial licenses can be obtained from the XESS Corp. web site
(www.xess.com) along with the NExS software and plug-ins for HP/UX, AIX,
Digital UNIX, SunOS, Solaris and Linux platforms.

