-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Announcing FileRunner 2.2.1 - a filemanager with built-in FTP.

List Of Nice Features:
======================

  * Easy, quick usage.
  * History of the last visited directories.
  * Hotlist, allows you to save often-visited locations.
  * Recursive Hyper-Menu of the entire file directory tree for quick 
    directory traversing.
  * Can browse FTP directories as easy as normal directories.
  * FTP capabilities:
    - Copy to and from FTP files or directories (recursive).
    - FTP Delete (recursive), FTP Makedir, FTP Rename.
    - Rule based configuration of FTP site logins. Set up
      simple rules for which sites are anon FTP and which 
      require user/password etc.
    - Supports FTP through proxy.
  * Asynchronous file operations (background execution). Includes
    FTP transfers.
  * Built-in command shell windows. Synchronized with file panels.
    These have history, aliases and file name completion.
  * Extendable by adding your own command buttons.
  * Very configurable.
  * User-defined file-pattern/actions. (*.jpg -> launch image viewer etc.)

  New in 2.2:
  * Find Files function for both Unix files and FTP sessions.
  * Chmod (change file permissions) GUI function.
  * Copy with resume for FTP. Let's you continue an FTP transfer that
    was previously aborted.
  * History of visited directories is now saved to disk.
  * Background execution of all shell commands.
  * And lots more of minor enhancements and bug fixes. 
    (See the online Help->History)

  New in 2.2.1:
  * Various smaller bug fixes.


Where to find it:
=================

ftp://ftp.x.org/contrib/utilities/FileRunner_2.2.1.tar.gz

Usually, FileRunner is also available at the following sites:
http://www.cd.chalmers.se/~hch/filerunner.html (screenshot here as well)
ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/FileRunner_x.x.tar.gz
ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/X11/xutils/managers/FileRunner_x.x.tar.gz

Requirements
============

FileRunner uses Tcl/Tk 7.6/4.2 and needs an ANSI C compiler to be
recompiled.

Pre-compiled libraries exist for Linux, SunOS 4.1.x and Solaris 2.5
(included in the archive).

FileRunner should run on any Unix/X11 platform and has been tested on:

 - Linux 2.0.x ELF with an ELF gcc compiler
 - SunOS 4.1.4 with the acc compiler
 - Solaris 2.5 with the cc compiler
 - Irix 5.3
 - UnixWare-2.x (Intel-SVR4.2MP)
 - HP-UX
 - Dec Alpha OSF (Digital Unix) 3.2
 - FreeBSD 2.1.5.
 - SCO OpenServer v5.0
 - AIX
 - NetBSD


Mailing list
============

There is a FileRunner announcement mailing list. Tell me if you want
to be on it.


FileRunner is Postcardware/Shareware
====================================

If you use FileRunner for non-commercial use, the cost is only a cool
postcard from you. If you use it for commercial use, it is US$20 per
user. See detailed information in the User's Guide where you will also
find my address.

