                                                              Product Release
                                                             January 20, 1997


                    CRYSTAL LAN(tm) ETHERNET INTERFACE DRIVER
                        for the LINUX OPERATING SYSTEM


Adding to the family of Crystal LAN(tm) device drivers for the
CS8900 and CS8920 ISA Ethernet controllers, Crystal Semiconductor
is pleased to announce the release of a CS8900/20 network
interface driver for the Linux operating system.

The "cs89x0" Linux network interface driver supports both
the version 1.2.13 and version 2.X.X Linux kernels.  It may
be compiled directly into the Linux kernel or compiled into a
loadable device driver module and loaded at run-time under either
kernel version.  The driver is designed to support all CS8900 and
CS8920-based adapter designs including the IBM Etherjet adapters.

The driver is distributed as a single-file archive (available
as a DOS .ZIP file or Linux .tar file) including source code
files,  a "cs89x0.o" pre-compiled loadable device driver module
(for the ver. 2.X kernel), and documentation.  The driver and
source code are freely distributable as provided under the GNU
License Agreement.

The driver may be obtained by either downloading from Crystal's
World Wide Web site or by contacting Crystal CS89XX Technical
Support.


