-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hello,

I have developed a new pair of file transfer utilities for people who are
frustrated with the Zmodem tools. The SixPack protocol doesn't have many of
the usual bells and whistles (at least not yet), but it works in terrain where
other protocols get stuck---such as over a link that involves multiple telnets
and terminal server sessions. Highlights: this thing is a sliding window
protocol that can reconstruct out-of-sequence segments and can deal
with multiple holes. At the lowest layers, all data is encoded into printable
ASCII characters prior to transmission. The user can currently control
only the window size.

Give SixPack a try and please send your comments to kaz@cafe.net.


