-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

I'm starting a new users group in Evansville, Indiana.  Topics for
meetings will include anything UNIX-related (including Linux), most
Internet-related technologies, plus Windows NT.

Since Linux is my primary OS (and my favorite, of course), I will be
discussing Linux topics most of the time.  In the nearly two and a
half years I've been running the Southern Illinois Linux Users Group,
I've found that we tend to get away from Linux-specific material much
of the time, but calling the group the Southern Illinois _Linux_ Users
Group kept many other UNIX-using individuals away.  I don't want that
to happen to this group, hence the name, the Evansville Advanced
Systems Users Group.

Of course, the more Linux users we have there, the better.  :-)

Following is the press release:

LOCAL USERS GROUP TO SUPPORT INTERNET TECHNOLOGIES

EVANSVILLE, Indiana    Jan. 20, 1997    Steven Pritchard, President
and Founder of the Southern Illinois Linux Users Group and Owner of
LANscape, a local Internet Consulting firm, today announced the start
of the Evansville Advanced Systems Users Group.  The EASUG will be
devoted to supporting the needs of UNIX, Windows NT, and Internet
users and professionals in the Evansville area.

Meetings will be held on the second Wednesday of every month starting
on February 12, 1997 at Red Bank Branch Library in Evansville.  Plans
for future meetings include talks about various UNIX, Windows NT, and
Internet related technologies, including visits by various vendors.
Plans are under way to invite representatives from Digital, Sun, IBM,
Microsoft, Novell, Caldera, and other vendors to demonstrate products
and discuss technical details of their products.

Call for Volunteers
- -------------------

Volunteers are needed to speak at meetings, work on the group's web
site, and otherwise help with the day-to-day operation of the group.

For more information, please visit the EASUG web site at
www.easug.org.  In addition, those wanting to be kept abreast of the
latest developments should subscribe to the users group's
announcements mailing list by sending email to majordomo@easug.org
with "subscribe easug-announce" in the body.

