-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Gr_monitor draws 3D color bar graphs of all processes on a Linux or SGI
IRIX system grouped by user.  By default it shows bars for CPU, resident
set size, memory, and elapsed time.  Visualize your system! 

This version is the same as the one I posted a while back, but updated for
Linux 2.0, and I've added a data gather for SGI IRIX (tested on 5.3, 6.2). 

Bars are continuously updated by a piped data feed - which can be from a
remote machine via rsh.  The data feed provides the row/column specs, so
you can write new kinds of feeds in C, Python.  You could even feed it
pre-recorded data from a file. 

The user interface is crude, but you can do things like scale and disable
bars, or rotate or translate the entire display via the keyboard. 

Screen dump preview at http://www.actrix.gen.nz/users/michael/giveaways.html

I don't have much time to work on gr_monitor.  If someone else feels like
improving it - or doing it right - please feel free to run with the ball.

I've placed a tar containing Linux/SGI source and Linux binaries at
   ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/gr_monitor-5.3.tar.gz

The following LSM entry details its final location

