xchklogsrc	Resource file for GUI

ck_uutraf   	Plug-out for UUCP			(v1.1)
ck_xferlog  	Plug-out for FTP			(v1.1)
logsummary  	Plug-out for Majordomo			(v1.1)
uusummary	part of ck_uutraf			(v1.1)

1.2 What's new in this version 
- ------------------------------

+ The 'execute' interface has been enhanced, now you can pass parameters
  to the program to execute. If %L is one of the parameters it is
  replaced by the absolute pathname of the log.

+ A shell script to guide user during installation to minimize configuration
  problems, it probes your system and advises you what has to be
  configured.

+ TIME oriented log expiration. Up to now it was only possible to specify
  maximum sizes (in bytes). As of this version you can *also* specify
  (mixing allowed) an age (in days or months) instead of a size. For
  exampe 8d (8 days) or 3m (3 months).

+ It is also possible to use the `k' or 'K' modifier for log sizes
  meaning Kilobytes.

+ Syslogd control is now done intelligently. Previously syslogd was
  stopped before processing all the logs and restarted afterwards, now
  it is done only if the current log is a syslogd log thus minimizing
  the syslogd 'down' time. Group them together (the syslog logs) and
  it is even better. [ You must configure $syslogConf for the probe
  to work! ]

+ Enhanced configuration file (chklogs.conf) syntax

+ Logical Groups of logs are now supported. You can create log groups,
  give it a name, specify which program (+params) to execute *before*
  checking the group (Pre) and *after* (Post) these need not to be the
  same. Useful if you need to control other things/daemons.

+ Directory processing. Some sites have a large amounts of logs of the
  same category such as UUCP logs for their leaf sites. Now it is 
  possible to specify a directory and every non-archive normal file
  under that directory is considered a log, no need to specify each
  of them.

+ Global and Local repositories. Before chklogs would let the created
  archives in the same directory where the log resided, thus cluttering
  the directory. With global options you can set whether you want your
  archives to reside in an OldLogs subdirectory just below the current
  one (local option) or in a global, grouped hierarchy somewhere else
  (global option + global spec).

+ Chklogs Administrative Program introduced. In order to support the
  new features and to facilitate interaction with chklogs the 
  chklogsadm program was created, it has several commands to control
  the configuration and operation of chklogs. It also relieves the
  cron'ed part (chklogs) from these tasks, less interpreting to do at
  work time. You must use this program or chklogs will not work as
  you want/expect. This is also needed in view of the future 
  developments of chklogs.
  
+ Chklogs Library. Contains common code and configuration variables
  needed by chklogs and chklogsadm. Also useful for 'execute' scripts.

+ Section 5 manual page (configuration file format), and manual page
  for chklogsadm (administrative program). I plan to stop making man
  pages with groff and use HTML instead, it's the 90's :-)

+ Rewrote this file completely (chklogs.txt).

+ Some Plug-outs for 'execute' logs

+ Graphical User Interface (work in progress)

+ Makefile to install software

+ Calling out for Plug-out and Pre/Post contributors.


1.3 Problems Solved
- -------------------

- - Empty lines in the configuration file no longer cause unnecessary
  lines (no name and zero values) in the reports. This was noticeable
  with -t and -w options.

- - When user didn't configure chklogs as specified in documentation (!),
  in particular $syslogF chklogs would attempt to stop a process with
  ID 0 (!!!) causing chklogs to go zombie, or crashing with stack fault,
  or going into background and other weird things. Of course all of
  that was because of wrong configuration. Anyway, now proper checking
  is done and this will not happen even if wrongly configured :-)

- - Changed some regular expressions, changed the header of the report,
  new trailer, renaming of some variables.


			Enjoy!
					Emilio
