Read news off-line with suck and any spool-aware news reader.

pnews (not Pnews) 0.12 has now been released.

pnews is a personal news spooling system. It is intended to allow you
to read news off-line with any Unix news reader that can read from a
local news spool [1]

Naturally, you can do this with suck and INN, but INN is a bit
overkill when used solely for off-line news reading by a single (or
even a few) user(s). pnews is intended to provide a simpler answer.

pnews, suck and rpost (part of the suck package) can be used in
conjunction with cron and diald (a great program that will dial your
phone and start SLIP/PPP for you) as a totally automated news
system. Just log in any time and fire up your news reader to read the
articles that spooled by cron and pnews. Outgoing articles can be
spooled and sent out in batches as well.

I considered pnews 0.10 and 0.11 to be alpha test, but I think we can
consider 0.12 to be a bit more than that. I expect to have 1.0 out
fairly soon (by my standards, remember that it's taken a bit over a
year to get from nothing to 0.12).

You can get pnews at:

http://www.holli.com/~jbuchana/computer.html

[1] After release 1.0 of pnews, I intend to start work on a simple
NNTP server so that people who would prefer not to read news directly
from a news spool may connect to a local NNTP server.


