- -----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

NetKit-0.09 has been uploaded to ftp.uk.linux.org (in
/pub/linux/Networking/base) and sunsite.unc.edu (in
/pub/Linux/Incoming.) 

This release supersedes NetKit-B-0.08 as well as earlier versions of
NetKit-B.

NOTE: There was a "NetKit-B-0.07B" uploaded to some archive sites. It
was *not* an official release and might be trojanized. Do not use it.
Please delete it if you see it anywhere.

*** This release fixes serious security problems in ftp, finger, and
*** rexecd. It also fixes a not-quite-so-serious security problem in
*** virtually all of the included programs. It is at best unwise to
*** continue to use older versions.

As of version 0.09, the "B" is gone from NetKit, on the grounds that
it no longer has much meaning and adds confusion. There used to be a
NetKit-A, but that has not existed for some time now.

This release of NetKit now includes routed, rpc.bootparamd, and
write/writed with network support.

NetKit-0.09 contains the following:

		biff  comsat  finger  fingerd  ftp  inetd  ping  
		rlogin  rlogind  rcp  rsh  rshd  rpcgen  rusers  
		rpc.rusersd  rwall  rpc.rwalld  rpc.bootparamd
		rpcinfo  routed  rwho  rwhod  talk  talkd  telnet  
		telnetd  timed  timedc  write  writed

It also contains rexecd, tftp, and tftpd, which should not be
installed unless needed.

This is a source-only release. Requires libc 5.2 or higher; 5.4 is
recommended. Should work with any kernel released within the last year
or two. Please get gcc-2.7.2 with the strength-reduce bug fix if you
don't already have it. Also requires ncurses. GNU readline is
optional.

Please send questions and comments to dholland@hcs.harvard.edu.


