Buy NExS for UNIX, Get NExS for Linux Free!

Release Date: 12/27/96

For a limited time, X Engineering Software Systems is offering any
customer purchasing a NExS Spreadsheet Professional Edition license
a free NExS Personal Edition license for Linux.

XESS Corp. President Tom Miller stated:

	``A drawback of UNIX in the workplace has been the
	impracticality of having a system at home which runs
	the same applications.  Linux appears to be emerging
	as the ``home system'' of choice for mainstream UNIX
	users.  This promotion lets our customers use the same
	high quality, affordable NExS spreadsheet on their
	Linux PC at home as they do on their UNIX workstation
	in their office.''

NExS, the Network Extensible Spreadsheet, is a full-featured, graphical
spreadsheet developed specifically for UNIX and the X Window System.
NExS has more than 200 built-in business and scientific functions,
allows user-customized functions, displays data using 2 and 3 dimensional
graphs, and imports and exports data in a wide variety of formats
(including HTML tables).

In addition, the conNExions application programming interface (API) gives
external processes complete control of NExS spreadsheets.  For example,
the API lets a remote data acquisition program transfer data over the
Internet to the NExS spreadsheet for real-time updates.  NExS can also
control the data-feed by communicating back to the remote process through
the API.  The conNExions API supports up to 63 of these simultaneous,
two-way connections.

NExS is available for HP/UX, AIX, Digital UNIX, SunOS, Linux, and Solaris
platforms.  Demonstration copies offering full functionality on
a limited number of cells may be downloaded from http://www.xess.com.
NExS is priced at \$149 for a single copy of the spreadsheet with the
conNExions API, and \$249 if a floating license is desired.
For information on the NExS spreadsheet and other products, visit
the XESS Corp. web site at http://www.xess.com.

