-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Etherboot-3.0b1 is a package containing code that can be put in a NIC
PROM to boot Linux diskless using bootp, tftp and/or NFS.

Many changes have been made since 2.1, mostly by Markus Gutschke, to
support new features; please see the LOG for details. The source tree
has also been reorganised.  A copy of Gero Kuhlmann's netboot-0.4 is
included. This is needed for the mknbi to construct the boot images.
Netboot-0.4 also has the beginnings of support for booting DOS over the
net.

If you intend to swap over NFS you will need to apply Claus Heine's
contributed patches to a 2.0.x kernel.

We have labelled it 3.0b1 because the changes are many and have not
been exhaustively tested, although we believe that they work.

It has been uploaded into ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming and
should show up at mirrors everywhere soon, normally in the
system/Linux-boot directory. In the meantime it is also available from
ftp://ftp.syd.dit.csiro.au/pub/ken/etherboot-3.0b1.{tar.gz,lsm}.

        Ken

Begin3
Title:          etherboot          
Version:        3.0b1
Entered-date:   10JAN97
Description:    Source for BOOT-Prom images; the code is based on the
                FreeBSD network-bootloader and supports loading of
                FreeBSD, Linux or DOS.  WD/SMC, NE1000/NE2000, 3COM
                3c503 and 3COM 3c509 are supported. There is optional
                code for supporting NICs based on Crystal Semiconductor's
                CS89x0 chipset.
Keywords:       booting, boot-rom, nfs, diskless, tftp, bootp
Author:         gutschk@math.uni-muenster.de (Markus Gutschke)
		ken@syd.dit.csiro.au (Ken Yap)
Maintained-by:  ken@syd.dit.csiro.au (Ken Yap) (primary maintainer)
		gutschk@math.uni-muenster.de (Markus Gutschke)
Primary-site:   sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/system/Linux-boot
                370967 etherboot-3.0b1.tar.gz
                1406 etherboot-3.0b1.lsm
Alternate-site: 
Original-site:  
Platforms:      An ELF-based GCC is required, EPROM burner recommended
                (unless booting from DOS disk). If building the 16 bit
		version, bcc from the Linux/16 or Linux/ELKS project is
		required. See src-16/README.16 for a more detailed
		description of src-16.
Copying-policy: Code by Markus Gutschke and Ken Yap are in the PUBLIC
		DOMAIN; but part of the code that this package is based
		on is BSD and other parts are GPL; read doc/COPYING for
		details!
