-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

This post to announce the first release of Freeciv.

Freeciv is a strategy game for X11, somewhat(to say the least ;)
inspired by Microprose's Civilization/Civnet.

This initial release has no AI, so you have to play against your
friends.

It's known to work under Linux, IRIX and Solaris.

Uploaded to sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/ are:

            freeciv-1.0.tgz
and         freeciv-1.0.lsm

These should be moved to /pub/Linux/X11/games/networked soon.

It is also available at http://www.daimi.aau.dk/~allan/freeciv.html,
where you can find screenshots and various updates.

LSM entry:

Begin3
Title:          Freeciv
Version:        1.0
Entered-date:   January 8, 1996
Description:    Freeciv is a turn-based strategy game in which each
                player becomes leader of a civilization, fighting to 
		obtain the ultimate goal: 
		The extinction of all other civilizations.
                Currently there's only support for multi-playing.
Keywords:       game strategy civilization 
Author:         Allan Kjeldbjerg, Claus Gregersen, Peter Unold
Maintained-by:  pjunold@daimi.aau.dk (Peter Unold)
Primary-site:   sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/X11/games/networked
Alternate-site: http://www.daimi.aau.dk/~allan/freeciv.html
Original-site:  ftp://ftp.daimi.aau.dk/pub/stud/pjunold/freeciv-1.0.tgz
Platform:       X11
Copying-policy: GPL2
End

