-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hello linuxers,

Version 1.2 of my tcpsendexpect program is now available at sunsite.unc.edu
in /pub/Linux/Incoming, eventually moving to /pub/Linux/system/Network/misc.

TCPsendexpect let you to automatize connections over TCP/IP via a chat like
program. Some usage example are included.

Previous versions are bugged, please *destroy it* :-)

This is the LSM:

Begin3
Title:          TCP send expect chat
Version:        1.2
Entered-date:   14DEC96
Description:    tcpsendexpect is a program that connects to a TCP port of a
                host and make a chat. You can use it to automatize some
                operation on remote servers, for example I use it to emulate a
                connection via telnet to a Cisco terminal server for killing
                users that are not allowed. You can use it to retrieve
                e-mail or news from your host or to make some remote
                operations, sending commands directly to a login session. You
                can use to write simple clients for some internet protocols,
                for example a single line WWW page retriever (I use it
                to retrieve meteo maps via crontab) or a simple pop client
                writted in shell language.
Keywords:       chat tcp socket www html
Author:         beppe@profuso.com (Giuseppe Zanetti)
Maintained-by:  beppe@profuso.com (Giuseppe Zanetti)
Primary-site:   sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/system/Network/misc
                9k tcpsendexpect.1.2.tar.gz
Alternate-site: 
Original-site:  
Platform:       Linux
Copying-policy: GNU GPL
End


