NExS Version 1.3-BETA Available

Release Date: 1/12/97

X Engineering Software Systems (XESS Corp.) announces the immediate
availability of the BETA version of the NExS 1.3 spreadsheet for
Linux and UNIX workstations.

With the release of version 1.3-BETA, NExS now offers import of Excel files, 
increases its visualization capabilities wuth new graph types, and 
incorporates fixes for several known bugs in NExS 1.2.  A detailed list of 
the new features and changes is included below.

NExS, the Network Extensible Spreadsheet, is a full-featured, graphical 
spreadsheet developed specifically for UNIX and the X Window System.  
NExS has more than 237 built-in business and scientific functions, allows 
user-customized functions, displays data using 2 and 3 dimensional graphs, 
and imports and exports data in a wide variety of formats (including HTML 
tables).

In addition, the conNExions application programming interface (API) gives 
external processes complete control of NExS spreadsheets.  For example, 
the API lets a remote data acquisition program transfer data over the Internet 
to the NExS spreadsheet for real-time updates.  NExS can also control the 
data-feed by communicating back to the remote process through the API.  
The conNExions API supports up to 63 of these simultaneous, two-way 
connections.

Demonstration copies and additional conNExions plug-ins may be downloaded 
from http://www.xess.com.  NExS is priced at $149 for the Personal Edition, 
and $249 if a floating license is desired.


New Features in NExS 1.3-BETA
- -----------------------------
+ NExS now supports an Error graph type which plots a data line and the
  ``error band'' around each data point.

+ Error and Hi Lo graphs can now display their main data set using either
  lines, splines or bars.

+ Excel (5.0 or later) XLS file import has been implemented.

+ Four-digit years are now supported in the @DATE function.

+ Date/time check/conversion was added when importing text.


Bug Fixes from NExS 1.2 to NExS 1.3-BETA
- ----------------------------------------
+ Graph data set indexing now starts from 1 instead of 0 in error messages.

+ Distant points with large PostScript coordinates are now intelligently
  limited to values 10 x (maximum visible PostScript bbox dimension).
  You still won't see them (as you shouldn't),
  and this will prevent some PostScript interpreters from bombing.

+ Color fills in all graph types now respond to the ``fill style''
  option, so the colors can be muted by mixing in the background
  pixel color.

+ Fixed line drawing in X so that lines are capped exactly where they
  should end (no rounding of the line cap).

+ The joining at end-points on polygons in graphs was fixed so it's not jagged.

+ The alignment of the end-caps terminating the bars in Hi-Lo and
  Error graph types has been improved.

+ A thin bar always connects the end-caps in Error and Hi Lo graphs
  regardless of the user-selected width of the data line.

+ Stacked line and bar graphs with a logarithmic Y axis are now correctly
  aligned with respect to each other.

+ Creating stacked bar or line graphs containing breaks (blank cells)
  will now assume the blank cells are 0 instead of complaining about
  mixing incompatible data types.

+ Tic marks on the X axis of a histogram now line up with the
  histogram bin boundaries.

+ Plug-in programs that connect with NExS via the conNExions API
  can now determine if they are connected to a NExS spreadsheet
  or an Xess spreadsheet.

+ The ``About'' menu button now displays the license pop-up.

+ Added handling for WKS\_STRING and WKS\_PASSWORD.

+ Checking for the FLEX license was fixed.

+ The initial license display is suppressed if we have a floating
  license which doesn't expire.

+ The license pop-up now disappears after 3 seconds.

+ Added LCOPYRIGHT for license pop-up display.

+ Fixed "invisible text" edit window problem.

