Announcing the Linux Browser Project
====================================

The Linux Browser Project is a group of developers developing a world
wide
web browser for Linux and other platforms. It is our opinion that none
of
the web browsers currently available for Linux have fully maximized the 
capabilities of this operating system. The goal of this project is to
develop a web browser which consists of a modular program architecture 
based around a small, fast kernel which would load necessary modules on
demand. This would include separate modules for HTML interpretation, net
connectivity, and user interface and display, as well as making it easy
for other user added modules to be written for additional functionality.
In the end, the basic browser and "standard" modules should be able to
fit
on a 1.44MB floppy.

The project is in its early stages, and we are announcing the project at
the moment to make ourselves known to the rest of the Linux community.
If 
anyone would be interested in helping us out in any way, please feel
free 
to join the mailing lists or visit the web site and let us know that you 
are willing to help.

There are two mailing lists setup for discussing this project, you can
subscribe to them by sending mail to majordomo@charon.net.au with either
"subscribe linux-browser-disc" or "subscribe linux-browser-dev" in the
body. The linux-browser-disc list is for general discussion of the
project,
linux-browser-dev is for discussion of technical details among
developers.

More information about the project can be found on the Linux Browser 
Project home page at http://www.tjhsst.edu/LBP/.

        Thanks for your time,
                The Linux Browser Project Team
                Jason A. Miller (jasonm@trib.com) - Project Coordinator


