Note: I tried to upload this wrapper to ftp.redhat.com but it
seems like their Incoming directory is full! So in the mean time
you can find this wrapper at:

 ftp://ftp.phy.bnl.gov/pub/linux/redhat/bnl-RPMS-i386/

- --------------------------------------------------------------------

         *** Netscape Wrapper for linux with libXpm.4.6 fix ***

        Author: Dr. Stephen Adler
        e-mail: stephen.adler@bnl.gov
        CopyRight: Gnu CopyRight License
        Developed at: Brookhaven National Laboratory
        files: netscape-wrapper-bnl-3.01-0.i386.rpm
        ftp://ftp.phy.bnl.gov/pub/linux/redhat/bnl-RPMS-i386/

        Release 1 Update: Jan 13th, 1997
        If you have installed netscape-wrapper-bnl-3.01-0 goto
        the end of this file for an update notice.

I have put together an rpm package which will install Netscape on
a linux system running RedHat. In order to avoid copyright infringements
with Netscape, the rpm package does not contain Netscape. Rather,
you need to fetch your own copy of Netscape from the Netscape
ftp sites and put it in /tmp. Once done, you can execute rpm and
netscape-wrapper-bnl will, as a post installation step, untar
the contents of the Netscape tar file in the /tmp directory and
put the stuff in /usr/lib/X11/netscape/3.01.

This wrapper procedures installs a script I wrote which runs
netscape from a shell script called run_netscape. A soft link
is made between /usr/lib/X11/netscape/bin/run_netscape and
/usr/X11/bin/netscape so in the end, you just type netscape
in to execute it.

                   -- LINUX JAVA BUG FIX --

This wrapper procedure also installs libXpm.4.6 and libc.5.0.9
in /usr/lib/X11/netscape/3.01/lib with pointers to other standard
libraries and redefines LD_LIBRARY_PATH to point to this
directory, thus fixing the annoying java script bug plaguing
netscape 3.01. More details on this bug fix can be found at

     http://members.ping.at/theofilu/netscape.html

I hope this procedure is of help to those running RedHat Linux on
their PCs.

You will find the latest rpm files at

ftp://ftp.phy.bnl.gov/pub/linux/redhat/bnl-RPMS-i386

NOTE: netscape-wrapper-bnl expects to find the netscape gziped
tar file in the directory with this very long filename:

/tmp/netscape-v301-export.x86-unknown-linux-elf.tar.gz

The installation will fail if this file is not there.

Steve.

Netscape-Wrapper-3.01-1 update: (Jan 13th, 1997)

  There was a bug in release 0 of this netscape wrapper routine which
did not properly pass the netscape command line invoked by the user
to netscape proper. The fix was submitted by
Fozzy C. Dressel <fozzy@richie.co.at> to which I send my dearest
regards and thanks.

  Also, if you have already installed netscape-wrapper-bnl-3.01-0
and are going to upgrade to netscape-wrapper-bnl-3.01-1, you do
not need to re-fetch the netscape tar file
netscape-v301-export.x86-unknown-linux-elf.tar.gz. Release 1
of netscape-wrapper-bnl-3.01 will proceed to install the wrapper
script and Java bug fix libraries without touching the netscape
files already installed in /usr/lib/X11/netscape/3.01 if the
file /tmp/netscape-v301-export.x86-unknown-linux-elf.tar.gz is
not found. A warning message will be given that this file
was not found. Also you will see the message
'cannot remove /usr/lib/X11/netscape/3.01 - directory not empty'
after doing the upgrade which you should ignore.

