LOS ANGELES: 4Front Technologies is announcing the availability of Open
Sound System for Linux with full support for Creative Lab's Sound Blaster
AWE32 soundcard. OSS/Linux version 3.7.1 will support both digital audio
and the EMU8000 wavetable synthesizer on the SB AWE32. 4Front is also 
shipping a licensed copy of the SoundFont (TM) GM ROM definition file 
(SYNTHGM.SF2) from E-mu.

Currently, only the non-PnP version of the SB AWE32 is supported. Support 
for the  SB AWE32 PnP will be announced shortly.

4Front Technologies has licensed the EMU8000 wavetable synthesizer support 
from Mr. Takashi Iwai. With complete integration of the EMU synth driver 
into OSS/Linux, all the public domain AWE32 MIDI and MOD applications will 
run without modification.

OSS/Linux is a commercial implementation of the OSS/Free drivers (the free 
soundcard drivers provided with the Linux kernel distribution). OSS/Linux
offers an easy GUI based installation of the sound drivers. Recompiling
the Linux kernel to add audio support is no longer required. With its unique
autodetection of soundcards, OSS/Linux can configure most soundcards in a
matter of minutes. It also supports various Plug-n-Play (PnP) soundcards for
which there is no support in the OSS/Free kernel drivers.

Users can visit 4Front's WWW site at http://www.4front-tech.com/linux.html
to download a free 5-day trial version of OSS/Linux or buy a fully licensed 
version of OSS/Linux for only $20.00. The licensed version of OSS/Linux 
comes with free technical support and free updates to the drivers. All
current OSS/Linux customers requiring AWE32 support can get the AWE32 option
for free. There is a $10.00 fee for SB AWE32 support for all new customers.

