Hi there,

I made a simple but nice gadget. What follows is a shortened version of the
README file: 



  What is Ruplist?


Ruplist is a gadget that shows you (if connected to a Local Area Network)
(LAN) all sites on that LAN with their uptimes and their rankings. These 
rankings depend on the uptime of a site.


  How is it done?


Ruplist uses the 'ruptime' command and parses its output. It then compares
it with the last time ruplist was used. It then first gives the current
ranking of a site and after that it gives the ranking the site had last time
it was used. Ruplist is built for multi-users usage, so everybody has it own
campare file. 

There is more then only the current uptime top list. Ruplist also keeps a
list of the longest uptimes ever, since the first usageof ruplist. Updates
on the longest uptime list is done while running ruplist normally (or with
silent mode option). There are two ways the longest uptimes can be
displayed. See the manual file for more info.


  Requirements for ruplist to run properly

Ruplist has been developed on a Linux system running 1.3.x development
kernels and in the end Linux 2.0.0. I compiled it with the 2.7.0 and 2.7.2
gcc compiler. 


