It has been several months since the last update to diald-top.  I have been
given a lot of feedback, and unfortunately have not had the time to act on any
of the results.  *BUT* I had enough of the ncurses stupidity that caused
segfaults after buffers were 1024 bytes long, so I performed a bug-fix from
version 0.6.  The changes since v0.6 are:


 o Changed 0.1ms sleeps to 999.900ms sleeps after each screen update for even
	more CPU niceness.  Introduces a slight delay, but the CPU time goes
	WAY down.
 o Changed back to line buffering, but using dynamically allocated line
	buffers.  Should fix the annoying ncurses/seg fault bug.


I am not sure when the next revision is forthcoming, but as soon as I have the
time to parse all the fine mail I have received, I am sure to fix a lot more.
Keep the mail flowing.

Included in the archive is a prebuilt ELF binary that is dynamically linked
with ncurses-1.9.9e.  It was made with the Makefile in the archive.  Enjoy...

Please send any comments, bug reports or patches to:
	gjhurlbu@beirdo.uplink.on.ca




