ROOT -- An Object Oriented Framework for Large Scale Data Analysis

A few days ago we've released v0.9 of the ROOT system. A version
for Linux using LessTif 0.75 can be downloaded via our web site:
http://root.cern.ch/.

ROOT provides, a.o., a hierarchical OO database, container classes,
a C++ interpreter, advanced statistical analysis (multi dimensional
histogramming, fitting, minimization, cluster finding algorithms) and
visualization tools (2D, 3D graphics and PostScript). The user 
interacts with ROOT via a graphical user interface, the command line
or batch scripts. The command and scripting language is C++ (using
the C++ interpreter) and large scripts can be compiled and dynamically
linked in. The OO database has been designed for parallel access
(reading as well as writing) by multiple processes and supports
and efficient compression mechanism. The system  contains also a
powerful C++ documentation generator (all source code on the web
site is hyperized using this tool).

A few days ago we've released v0.9 of the ROOT system. A version
for Linux using LessTif 0.75 can be downloaded via our web site:
http://root.cern.ch/.

- -The main features of this new version can be found at:
     http://root.cern.ch/root/html/examples/V0.9.txt.html
Please, read this page carefully before upgrading from v0.8.

This new version is running on additional machines. See complete
list at:
     http://root.cern.ch/root/Availability.html#download

Dependence on the last commercial component has been removed. 
ROOT on Linux works now with LessTif v0.75 see:
     http://www.hungry.com/products/lesstif/

We provide the complete ROOT documentation in both html and Postscript
formats ready to browse or print at:
     http://root.cern.ch/root/Availability.html#documentation

The ROOT web site has been modified to include additional information
to start with ROOT. Of particular interest, the URL:
     http://root.cern.ch/root/Howto.html

If you are interested by ROOT Input/Output benchmarks, have a look at:
     http://root.cern.ch/root/Ebench.html


We hope you will have fun working with ROOT and welcome any suggestions,
comments and bug reports.


The ROOT Team,

