Hi,

Due to too much work, Dirk Edelbuettel
<Dirk.Eddelbuettel@qed.econ.queensu.ca> recently mailed me that he can no
longer maintain TOB. So I'm looking for a new maintainer.

TOB is driver for backup- and restore procedures. It's only a shell script
with some resource files, so bash-programming is a pro if you're considering
taking it over. The script calls the right programs at the right times so
that a backup is made, or a listing is shown, or so that files are restored. 

The maintenance has been somewhat neglected: TOB is functional, but requests
have come in and are available in saved emails. The maintainer would have to
browse through, and see what he/she could implement.

