Raima Corp. Ports High-Performance, Royalty-Free Raima Database
Manager++ To Linux OS

Issaquah, WA-December 16, 1996-Raima Corporation announced it is now
offering its Raima Database Manager++ high-performance database for the
Linux operating system. Now developers of applications for the
widely-used, Posix-compatible Linux can take advantage of proprietary
Raima technology such as low level C and C++ APIs, and support for the
relational database model, pointer-based network database model, and
combined database model.

For more than ten years, C and C++ developers have embedded RDM++
(formerly db_VISTA) in thousands of commercial and corporate in-house
applications. Companies with Raima-based applications include Hewlett
Packard, Pure Atria, Motorola, IBM, Cheyenne, Cybercash, Nasdaq, Fujitsu
and IDS Prof. Scheer.   Raima-based applications meet the needs of a
wide range of industries, including telephony/telecommunications,
finance, imaging and document management, and science/medicine.

Linux is a UNIX-like operating system introduced by Finnish programmer
Linus Torvalds in 1991 as a freely distributable product. Linux runs on
x86, Digital Alpha and Motorola PowerPC and 68k machines, and supports a
wide range of software and standards, including X Windows, Emacs, and
TCP/IP networking.  Linux has developed a loyal and large base of users,
and is considered to have performance comparable to that of the
well-known UNIX operating systems from major commercial vendors.  Both
the Linux OS and tools are available from many sources, including the
Free Software Foundation and firms such as Caldera and Red Hat.

Raima Database Manager++ is royalty-free-software companies buy a
development license, and can distribute run-time copies without any
charge. Raima's new Linux version of RDM++ adds to a long list of
supported platforms, including most UNIX variants, Windows (95/NT/3.1),
OS/2, and real-time operating systems such as QNX and VxWorks.
Cross-platform support is a boon to commercial application developers,
because it allows them to offer their products on additional operating
systems without extensive recoding.

Support for multiple database models is an RDM++ feature that enables
developers to create especially fast applications. Most commercially
available databases support only the relational database model.
Relational databases store data in tables, and queries often have to
join multiple tables, resulting in poor performance.  In addition,
relational data designs don't provide the flexibility to handle complex
data relationships efficiently.

Network database model technology-an alternative to the relational
database model-stores records in sets made up of owner and member
records. Because records in a set are physically joined, via pointers, a
query can find related information almost instantaneously, resulting in
much faster data lookups. Raima Corporation's database technology
supports databases that use the best features of both the relational and
network database models, to achieve a design that works best.

Raima's proprietary "d_" C API is another RDM++ feature that enables
developers to enhance their applications' performance. The API consists
of some 200 C functions for database manipulation and control.  RDM++
also includes Raima Object Manager, a class library that provides an
object-oriented interface to RDM++ by encapsulating database navigation
and object storage and retrieval into C++ classes.

Raima Corporation, with headquarters in Issaquah, Washington, is a
leading developer of high-performance database technology. In addition
to Raima Database Manager++, Raima also produces Velocis Database
Server, a client/server, ODBC SQL database; and Raima Object Manager, a
class library that encapsulates object storage and database navigation
in C++ classes, providing an object-oriented interface to Raima
databases.   The company also provides database reporting and analysis
tools; a Web Server interface to Velocis Database Server; and
consulting, Internet development, training and other services through
the company's Vista Development Corporation subsidiary.  For more
information on Raima, call 800 327-2462 (206 557-0200 internationally)
or visit its Web site at http://www.raima.com.

