As a thank-you to Linux users for making BRU(tm) for Linux such a success,
EST is offering BRU for Linux (full edition, $299 list) at a very special
price to members of Linux-oriented user groups around the world. 

Until February 15th, 1997, Linux user group members can purchase a full
release copy of BRU for Linux for $199.00.  This is $100 off of our
regular price of $299 - a savings of 33%.  This offer includes both the 
Intel and Alpha platforms.

About BRU
- ---------

BRU, the Backup and Restore Utility for UNIX and UNIX-Like systems, offers
the most reliable backup available for Linux and other UNIX environments. 
BRU is 100% device independent, so it works with all Linux supported
devices, including ftape, SCSI, IDE, MO, Iomega Jaz and Zip, Syquest
ezflyer and Syjet, disk files, or any other device that you can write to
and read from under Linux.

In addition to supporting standard Linux and UNIX filesystems, BRU will
properly backup and restore any available SMB volumes when using SAMBA
under Linux, including Microsoft Windows 3.11, WFW, 95 and NT, IBM OS/2,
and other SMB compatible filesystems.

Since recovery of the archived data is the PRIMARY reason to perform
backups, BRU provides three levels of verification for all BRU archives,
Autoscan(tm) verification, bit-level verification and Anytime Verify(tm). 
Since BRU's primary focus is on the reliability of the data written to the
archive, we ensure that the data that you THINK made it onto tape actually
DID make it. 

BRU for Linux is currently available for both Intel and DEC Alpha 
systems, and we are working on ports to SPARC and PowerPC systems.

