-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hi Linux power users worldwide,

I've uploaded the package acctsum 1.0 to ftp.inka.de and
sunsite.unc.edu. This is the first version which has only
be tested on two of my own systems with Linux 2.0.x.
However, it is in production use since several weeks here
and should be stable.

What Is It?

The acctsum package consists mainly of a shell script that evaluates
your accounting file and summarizes the information in it by days,
weekdays, months, and years. It normally mails its results to the
system administrator. It is intended to be run by cron once per day.

There's a second shell script that reports your ISDN usage and
truncates the ISDN log file. It is intended to be run by cron
once per month. You obviously must have an ISDN card and isdnlog
to use this.

Features

* Keeps your accounting file small. The accounting file is truncated
  after it is evaluated.

* Summarizes processes and their CPU usage by day, day of week, month,
  and year.

* Can mail the summary to the system administrator.

* Sorts the summary by programs and by users.

* Calculates ISDN fees.

The main use of these scripts may be the truncation of the log file,
but I hope there are other useful applications too - graphical
presentation of the results, or whatever.

