Merry Christmas all,

This is to announce the availability of pileup v1.0. This is a Linux
program aimed at Radio Amateurs with an interest in CW (Morse Code).
Pileup simulates the pileup tapes often heard at Amateur Radio
conventions. These are typically multi-track tapes with many CW stations
on and the winner is the person who can copy the highest number of
callsigns.

Pileup is based on sccw by Steve Merrifield (sjm@ee.latrobe.edu.au).

Pileup requirements
1. SoundBlaster compatible sound card (PC speaker not supported);

Pileup features in v1.0
1. CW speed can be selected
2. Number of stations calling at once (1 to 9) can be selected
3. CW speed of each station calling is different to simulate a CW pileup
4. Tone of each station calling is different to simulate the "spread" of
a CW pileup
5. Callsigns are from the log (3000 in all) of M6A in the 1996 CQ WW CW
contest to add some realism!

Pileup v1.0 can be found on
1. ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming (and hopefully
/pub/Linux/apps/ham)
2. http://www.babbage.demon.co.uk/pileup.html

Any suggestions/bugs etc please to Richard Everitt (G4ZFE)
richard@babbage.demon.co.uk

